-- Rule LendTool creates every Loan, with `dueOn` set to seven days from today. A member has a
-- late loan when one of its loans is due before today, so no loan is late on the day it is
-- created.
--
-- `velle compare` from an empty spec (an empty file) to this file prints, under "What that
-- changes", these lines among others. Each is followed in the report by its "In the spec:"
-- lines, left out here.
--
--   ### Member
--   - LendTool creating a Loan can now make a Member become a MemberWithLateLoan.
--   - Time passing can now make a Member become a MemberWithLateLoan.
--   - Time passing can now make a Member stop being a MemberWithLateLoan.
--
-- The first line cannot happen: the loan LendTool creates is due seven days after today, so
-- `dueOn < today` is false in the commit that creates it. The compiler does not read the value
-- the rule gives `dueOn`. A member becomes a MemberWithLateLoan by time passing, which the
-- second line already says. The third line is the case in
-- `34-compare-filtered-collection-direction-accepted.velle`.
act Member { name: text }

transient act Borrow { member: one Member }

shape Loan {
    member: one Member
    dueOn: Date
}

rule LendTool when Borrow {
    Loan from { member: member, dueOn: today + 7 days }
}

shape MemberWithLateLoan = Member where exists (loans where dueOn < today)
